}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mystic Egg: N111''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Cop Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Cop Cat is best described as a more aggressive, anti-Traitless [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]. Cop Cat has a lower cost, shorter recharge time and faster attack rate and animation, but does much less damage in exchange for significantly more HP due to having the [[Strong Against]] ability instead of [[Massive Damage]]. Against [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies, Cop Cat boasts absurd stats: 68k effective health and 6k DPS at level 30, which is very impressive for a unit that can be sent out every 14 seconds. Cop Cat's Behemoth Slayer is nothing to scoff at either, being able to do nearly 10k DPS against Behemoths while having around 50k effective HP. Since Behemoth Slayer stacks with Strong Against, Cop Cat's health and DPS reach jaw-dropping levels against Traitless Behemoths like [[Wild Doge]], [[Cumulus Gallus]] and [[Elephantidae Papaou]], allowing it to counter them very effectively.

Something to know about this unit is that it has relatively low survivability, due to only having two knockbacks. This means that when an enemy gets close to Cop Cat, they can shred a significant portion of their health since Cop Cat won't be knocked back to safety. You can use this to your advantage, though, as Cop Cat can hit fast attacking Traitless enemies such as [[Rain D.]] and [[R.Ost]] without being stunlocked.

The cherry on top for this unit is that Cop Cat also has better generalist stats than a [[Talents|Talentless]] and unboosted Pizza Cat, with marginally better HP and DPS, while also having lower cost, shorter cooldown, and faster attack rate and animation.

