==Trivia==
*111 is the emergency number in New Zealand, possibly explaining this unit's evolution into Cop Cat.
*Cop Cat can be seen as a foil to [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]]. Both are sunglasses-wearing ranged [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Egg]] units that have damage-increasing [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]] abilities and are implied to be incompetent at their jobs, with Cop Cat chewing hot-dog-flavored gum to stay awake as he patrols a city with a crime rate of 120% and Hitman Cat being questioned by police more times than he has killed his targets. They contrast in how their professions oppose each other and Cop Cat is a more defensive unit that deals lower damage faster and in a smaller area, with exactly double the health of Hitman Cat, Strong Against instead of Massive Damage, and a much shorter attack cycle. Cop Cat's range is also equal to Hitman Cat's blind spot.

